WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.111
The raster is a real 3D object, so it can be shown in real 3D.

2
00:00:05.111 --> 00:00:09.523
Three ways: anaglyph, side-by-side stereo, and WebXR headsets.

3
00:00:09.974 --> 00:00:12.227
Anaglyph is in the Virtual Camera section.

4
00:00:12.227 --> 00:00:14.803
Switch it on and grab some red and cyan glasses.

5
00:00:15.254 --> 00:00:17.930
Eye Sep sets how far apart the two eyes are.

6
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.634
More separation, more depth.

7
00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:21.337
Orbit the camera to feel it.

8
00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:28.800
For VR players and YouTube, the Record section can capture side-by-side stereo, with an optional 3D metadata tag.

9
00:00:29.256 --> 00:00:33.900
Preview stereo shows both eyes for three seconds, before you commit to a recording.

10
00:00:34.357 --> 00:00:42.112
With a WebXR headset connected, the XR section puts you inside the raster, at tabletop, room or architectural scale.

11
00:00:42.564 --> 00:00:44.793
Next: building a performance rig.
